message.content:
Below is a **step‑by‑step blueprint** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole flow – from planning to deployment – and sprinkle in code snippets, folder layouts, and tooling recommendations so you can jump straight into coding.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| Step | What to do | Why it matters |
|------|------------|----------------|
| **Define core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, product detail page, cart, checkout, user account, admin panel (optional). | Keeps scope focused. |
| **Create wireframes** | Use Figma/Sketch/Adobe XD. | Visualise layout before coding. |
| **Design UI kit** | Colors, typography, spacing, component library. | Consistency across pages. |
| **Accessibility audit** | WCAG 2.1 AA checklist. | Better UX & SEO. |
| **Performance goals** | First Contentful Paint < 2 s, Total Blocking Time < 200 ms. | Competitive edge. |

---

## 2. Tech Stack Choices

| Layer | Recommended Tech | Why |
|-------|------------------|-----|
| **Framework** | **React** (with Vite) or **Vue 3** (with Vite) | Component‑driven, huge ecosystem. |
| **State Management** | **Redux Toolkit** (React) or **Pinia** (Vue) | Predictable state, devtools. |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS** + **Headless UI** | Rapid styling, utility‑first. |
| **Component Library** | **Radix UI** (React) or **VueUse** | Accessible primitives. |
| **Routing** | **React Router v6** or **Vue Router 4** | Declarative routing. |
| **Form handling** | **React Hook Form** or **VeeValidate** | Lightweight, good validation. |
| **API client** | **Axios** or **fetch** + **React Query** | Caching, optimistic updates. |
| **Testing** | **Jest** + **React Testing Library** | Unit & integration tests. |
| **Linting/Formatting** | **ESLint**, **Prettier**, **Stylelint** | Code quality. |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions or GitLab CI | Automated tests & deploy. |
| **Hosting** | **Vercel** or **Netlify** | Edge functions, instant rollbacks. |

> **Tip:** If you’re already comfortable with a different stack (e.g., SvelteKit, Next.js), feel free to swap in the equivalent tools.

---

